        In everyday language, <em>mass</em> and <em>weight</em> are frequently treated as synonyms. However, in physics and mechanical engineering, they represent distinct physical quantities:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Mass (m):</strong> A scalar property representing the fundamental quantity of matter inside an object. It remains constant regardless of where the object is located in the universe, and is measured in <strong>kilograms (kg)</strong> and <strong>grams (g)</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Weight (W):</strong> A vector force representing the gravitational pull acting on that mass: <code>W = m × g</code>, where <em>g</em> is local gravitational acceleration (approximately <code>9.80665 m/s²</code> at Earth's sea level). Scientifically, weight is measured in <strong>Newtons (N)</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Because all standard commercial scales operate in Earth's relatively uniform gravitational field, scales measure gravitational force and display it directly calibrated as mass in kilograms or pounds. This tool serves as a practical everyday mass and weight converter for commercial, academic, and domestic applications.
      </p>

      <h2>Gold Weight Converter: Troy Ounces vs Standard Avoirdupois Ounces</h2>
      <p>
        When buying, selling, or valuing gold, silver, platinum, or palladium bullion, standard kitchen and grocery scales should never be used without adjustment because precious metals are weighed under the <strong>Troy weight system</strong>:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1 Troy Ounce (oz t) = exactly 31.1034768 grams</strong> (480 troy grains).</li>
        <li><strong>1 Standard Avoirdupois Ounce (oz) = exactly 28.349523125 grams</strong> (437.5 grains).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A Troy ounce is approximately <strong>9.707% heavier</strong> than an everyday household ounce. If you weigh gold on a standard postal scale reading 1.00 oz, that represents only 0.9115 Troy ounces of precious metal! Always use our dedicated <strong>Gold Weight Converter</strong> section above to ensure accurate bullion valuation.
      </p>

      <h3>Tola in Indian & South Asian Bullion Markets</h3>
      <p>
        In India, Pakistan, Nepal, and Middle Eastern gold souks, gold is traditionally traded in <strong>Tolas</strong>. Under standard metric definitions, <strong>1 Tola = exactly 11.6638038 grams</strong> (approximately 0.375 Troy ounces or 180 troy grains).
      </p>

      <h2>Height Weight Converter: Understanding the Relationship via BMI</h2>
      <p>
        Users often look for a <strong>height weight converter</strong>. It is important to recognize that <em>height</em> (a 1-dimensional measurement of length in centimeters or feet) and <em>weight</em> (a 3-dimensional measurement of mass in kilograms or pounds) cannot be directly converted into one another. A length of 175 cm does not correspond to a specific weight without an object's density and volume.
      </p>
      <p>
        However, in health science, nutrition, and medical diagnostics, height and weight are combined to determine:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Body Mass Index (BMI):</strong> <code>BMI = Weight (kg) / [Height (m)]²</code></li>
        <li><strong>WHO Healthy Weight Range:</strong> The normal weight boundaries corresponding to a BMI between 18.5 and 24.9 kg/m².</li>
        <li><strong>Ideal Body Weight (IBW):</strong> Formula-based guidelines (such as Devine or Robinson formulas) used by physicians and dietitians.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can use our integrated <strong>Height Weight & BMI Tool</strong> above to calculate your BMI and healthy target weight range based on your exact height.
      </p>

